 "source": {
  "map": "City of Sandy Zoning Map, 11 x 17 edition (Ordinance 2025-01, updated 2026-04-30), stored as or/clackamas/sandy/zoning-map-2026.map-only.pdf (sha256 401a4fad84bd6ed4be1a509228baad180f647c7f8754246eb9d0cc40e19b2fdb); a raster page, no vector linework",
  "quote": "or/clackamas/sandy/17.54/17.54.60.txt#L4",
  "says": "as shown on the City of Sandy Zoning Map",
  "inputs": {
   "taxlots": "Clackamas County taxlots served by the City of Wilsonville GIS (taxlot layer 11, EPSG:2913, fetched 2026-10-31), used to register the raster and for the check",
   "zoning": "Sandy zoning in the regional fabric (maps.orcity.org, 128 polygons, fetched 2026-10-31), used for the zone counts only"
  },
  "traced_by": "Claude (districts chunk 9 worker)",
  "traced_on": "2026-10-31",
  "drawn": true,
  "how": "The map draws the Bornstedt Village Overlay as a hatched area (17.54.00 E: a border and a letter S). The page was rendered to a raster, the thin diagonal hatch strokes picked out by colour and stroke width (the thick dashed urban growth boundary rejected by width), and the hatch closed into one solid region (a 25 pixel closing, about 128 ft) with its label holes filled. The raster was registered to EPSG:2913 by a similarity transform (5.12 ft per pixel, 1.3 degrees of rotation, a shift) fitted to the county taxlot lines: 82 percent of points sampled every 8 ft along those lines fall within a pixel of a drawn taxlot line, against 5 percent before fitting. The traced region is then grown 30 ft outward, so that a lot the hatch edge or the registration might misplace is cut by the line (unanswered) rather than read outside.",
  "check": "Of the taxlots near the line, 727 read inside (C3 3, R1 320, R2 158, R3 127, SFR 94, unzoned 25), 22 are cut and unanswered, and the rest read outside. The region holds the Cascadia Village subdivisions, which 17.54.60 exempts from 17.54.70-17.54.110; they are read inside, the stricter side, for the rules only hold.",
  "reading": "A lot is inside only when at least 90 percent of it lies within the line and outside only when at most 10 percent does (flats.geom.drawn); a lot the line cuts is unanswered and held open with FACT-SANDY-BORNSTEDT-VILLAGE (Bornstedt Village edge unconfirmed), never GREEN on the overlay's rules. The overlay's rules here only tighten (row-house lot widths), so the outward 30 ft can hold a lot, never release one.",
  "acres": "233.1"
 },
